><surname>Ebihara</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Infection of naive target cells with virus-like particles: implications for the function of ebola virus VP24.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>7260</fpage><lpage>7264</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16809331</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005308-Bray1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bray</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Geisbert</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmaljohn</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Huggins</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>A mouse model for evaluation of prophylaxis and therapy of Ebola hemorrhagic fever.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><volume>178</volume><fpage>651</fpage><lpage>661</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9728532</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005308-McConnell2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McConnell</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Imperiale</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Biology of adenovirus and its use as a vector for gene therapy.</article-title><source>Hum Gene Ther</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>1022</fpage><lpage>1033</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15610603</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005308-Reed1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohamadzadeh</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Status and challenges of f